        <property name="toolTip">
         <string>Scope — which objects Bake Lightmaps acts on.

Selected (default) — the current selection.
Visible — every visible mesh in the scene.
Scene — every mesh in the scene, hidden or not.</string>
        </property>
        <property name="frame">
         <bool>false</bool>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item>
       <widget class="ComboBox" name="cmb002">
        <property name="minimumSize">
         <size>
          <width>180</width>
          <height>19</height>
         </size>
        </property>
        <property name="maximumSize">
         <size>
          <width>999</width>
          <height>19</height>
         </size>
        </property>
        <property name="toolTip">
         <string>Packing — how the baked maps are laid out.

Per-Object (default) — one lightmap texture per object at the full Resolution. Best per-object detail; right for hero assets or small selections.

Atlas by Material — objects sharing a primary material are consolidated into one shared EXR (Resolution becomes the shared atlas size), and each object gets an area-weighted atlas rect bound at engine time (Unity's lightmapScaleOffset / glTF KHR_texture_transform) — UVs are never edited, and instances are fully supported: every copy keeps its own rect and its own lighting. Fewer textures, no naming collisions, more efficient texel use for many small objects. Bake-full-then-pack, so the bake quality is unchanged.</string>
        </property>
        <property name="frame">
         <bool>false</bool>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
